{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>שפרה</b> — The heh is added, and its meaning is 'formed' from שפר, or from שפרירו. Or the bet in the word ברוחו is added, and the dagesh in the peh of שפרה is absent." "<b>נחש בריח</b> — The sea-serpent that is in the sea. And some say: it is the constellation Draco [lit. the hanged one], and it is called 'snake' because it is like a coiled shape and a bar [בריח], for it extends [מבריח] from one end to the other end."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:03:42.628477272Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}